Subject: [PATCH] Schedule LP efficiency cores in the shared stream config

When a process affinity mask leaves only LP efficiency cores,
update_executor_config() omitted LP_EFFICIENT_CORE_PROC from the little-core
count and allocation types. With more than one requested stream, the table
could remain empty and its first-element access aborted GPU compilation.
Reported upstream as openvinotoolkit/openvino issue 39088.

Count LP cores as little cores, allocate them independently for ANY_CORE and
ECORE_ONLY, and keep PCORE_ONLY free of LP cores when P cores are available.
Choose the largest requested stream width that the eligible per-core-kind,
per-NUMA-node pools can supply. Skip smaller unused pools rather than reducing
otherwise feasible streams or emitting partial homogeneous rows. This also
preserves explicit P-core requests when an unused SMT pool is smaller.

Contribution rows after an ALL_PROC header carry zero streams. The zero-stream
helper selects LP cores before hyperthreads, and an empty generated table
raises a clear exception instead of reading element zero. Precomputed tables
are unchanged. No-LP behavior is preserved except for the intended correction
to mixed-stream contribution accounting.

Keep generated unpinned ECORE_ONLY streams homogeneous: the existing arena
interface cannot express an E/LP union. A single LP contribution becomes a
typed row with its original locality. Correct singleton TBB type selection
for the ordered [LP, E] pair only when the original table contains both
efficient kinds and no P/HT cores; preserve existing no-LP, P-present,
three-type and automatic mappings. Pinned mixed streams retain
their observer-based binding. This does not add a new TBB union mode.

Native regression tests cover LP-only preferences, reservation, pinning,
fragmented pools, NUMA, default factories, arena routing, noncontiguous TBB
type IDs and precomputed tables. The source
guard runs after %prep; it does not replace these behavioral tests.
Upstream acceptance remains open. Drop this patch when a release carries the
corresponding fix.

